                <pb facs="0586" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/2061: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Childs</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-16T22:00:00-05:00">December 16, 1941—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>159. Your 372, November 28, 1 p.m. In view of the apparent uncertainty of the
                    precise purpose of the Delegate’s note, the Department feels that the first and
                    last paragraphs of your proposed reply constitute an adequate acknowledgment and
                    offer of cooperation. However, it is suggested that in the last paragraph the
                    word “adjusting” be substituted for the phrase “my informal endeavors to
                    adjust”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
